==English==
[[File:Mol2D.L.Methionine.png|right|thumb|Structure diagram of methionine]]
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{term|methyl|me(thyl)}} + {{term|thio-|lang=en}} + (euphonic) ''-n-'' {{suffix||ine|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/mɪˈθʌɪəniːn/|/mɪˈθʌɪənɪn/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|amino acid|organic compound||lang=en}} A [[lipotropic]], [[sulphur]]-[[containing]] [[essential amino acid]], C<sub>5</sub>H<sub>11</sub>NO<sub>2</sub>S, found in most [[protein]].
#* '''1999''', {{w|Matt Ridley}}, ''Genome'', Harper Perennial 2004, p. 253:
#*: The purpose was to make soya beans more healthy for those for whom they are a staple food by correcting soya beans' natural deficiency in a chemical called '''methionine'''.

